   877	/*
   878	 Interrupt disabling strategy:
   879	 If the source is >=0 (meaning a muxed interrupt), we disable it by muxing the interrupt to a non-connected
   880	 interrupt. If the source is <0 (meaning an internal, per-cpu interrupt), we disable it using ESP_INTR_DISABLE.
   881	 This allows us to, for the muxed CPUs, disable an int from the other core. It also allows disabling shared
   882	 interrupts.
   883	 */
